        "texts": {
          "summary": "UserTable (memo) re-renders with 150 UserRow below it on every click: prop `columns` is a new array each render with the same value, created at UserAdmin.tsx:14. Wasted: about 15.3 ms per click. Fix: move it out of the component, since it uses nothing from it, or wrap it in useMemo (React Compiler would do this automatically).",
          "why": "memo only skips a render when every prop is the same object as last time. `columns` looks the same, but it's a new array on every render, so UserTable and everything below it re-renders for nothing.",
          "line": "`columns={['name', 'email', 'role']}` at UserAdmin.tsx:14.",
          "fix": "It uses nothing from the component, so move it outside, to the top of the file: `const COLUMNS = ['name', 'email', 'role'];`, then pass `columns={COLUMNS}`. UserTable then gets the same array on every render. Wrapping it in useMemo also works: `const columns = useMemo(() => ['name', 'email', 'role'], []);`. React Compiler would do this automatically."
        },
        "rank": 1
